## C. Graph model, data and methodology (2:50)

### C1 · Graph model (5:15–6:05)
- **G = (V, A)**, a complete **directed** weighted graph.
- **V** = {V0, …, V{{n_hospitals}}}: {{n}} vertices (1 depot + {{n_hospitals}} hospitals).
- **A** = every ordered pair (i, j), i ≠ j: **{{n_arcs}} arcs** = the drive from i to j.
- **Weight w(i, j)** = driving distance **in km** ({{distance_source_short}}).
- **Why directed:** {{asym_pairs}} of the {{n_pairs}} pairs have d(i,j) ≠ d(j,i) (one-way streets, U-turn rules, bridges).
- Visual: `fig1_graph.png` (vertex labels only; the weights are on the next slide).

### C2 · Weight matrix and data sources (6:05–6:55)
- Visual: `fig2_weight_matrix.png` (row = FROM, column = TO).
- **Sources:** {{distance_method}}. Coordinates: {{coord_source}}.
- **Actual vs assumed:** {{status_summary}} (`data/data_sources.csv`). Assumed cells are hatched and marked * in the matrix.
- Quality checks: {{asym_pairs}} of {{n_pairs}} pairs differ by direction; {{triangle_breaks}} triangle-inequality breaks above 0.1 km, listed in `outputs/data_quality.csv` and checked by hand (one-way streets, not typos).
- The validator checks: square matrix, zero diagonal, positive distances, ids match `locations.csv`, matrix = `data_sources.csv`.

### C3 · Methodology and parameter choice (6:55–7:45)
- Pipeline: CSVs → validator → graph (networkx) → **SA** → verification → brute force + greedy (same matrix) → 30 runs → figures.
- Parameters (`src/config.py`):

| Parameter | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| T0 | {{t0}} km | auto: an average worse move ({{mean_uphill}} km) is accepted with P = {{target_p}} at the start |
| α | {{alpha}} | sensitivity study below |
| moves per level | {{ipt}} | about {{ipt_ratio}}× the {{n_swaps}} possible swaps of {{n_hospitals}} hospitals |
| T_stop | {{t_stop}} km | {{t_stop_reason}} |
| patience | {{patience_levels}} levels | no new best while T falls {{patience_drop}}× |
| seed | {{seed}} | reproducible run for the video |

- Why not the paper's defaults (T0 = 1000, α = 0.995, 1000 moves/level, T_stop = 1e-8)? T0 = 1000 ignores the units (km), and on our data {{paper_defaults_short}}
- α sensitivity ({{sens_runs}} runs per value, same seeds): `fig9_alpha_sensitivity.png`

{{alpha_table}}


### C4 · Implementation: main code components (7:45–8:05)
| Module (`src/`) | Role |
|---|---|
| `data_loader.py` | read and validate the CSVs (square, zero diagonal, positive, ids) |
| `graph_model.py` | networkx DiGraph; `tour_cost()` sums the arcs of a closed tour |
| `simulated_annealing.py` | **the algorithm**: `random_tour`, `swap_two_cities`, `metropolis`, `simulated_annealing` |
| `baselines.py` | brute force (Alg 2.3) and greedy (Alg 2.7) on the same matrix |
| `verify.py` | tour rules + independent edge-by-edge recount |
| `experiments.py`, `visualize.py`, `maps.py` | 30 runs, α study, figures and maps |

The core of `simulated_annealing()`, shortened (trace and history lines left out; in the file every line is commented with its Alg 2.5 step):
```python
for _ in range(params.iterations_per_temperature):   # inner loop
    new_tour, positions = make_move(current, rng)     # step 4
    new_cost = tour_cost(new_tour, D)                 # step 5
    delta = new_cost - current_cost
    accepted, p, r = metropolis(delta, T, rng)        # steps 6-10
    if accepted:
        current, current_cost = new_tour, new_cost
        if current_cost < best_cost:                  # best-so-far (step 13)
            best, best_cost = current.copy(), current_cost
T *= params.alpha                                     # step 11
```

